62fdbde1]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.1.stable - macOS Sequoia (15.7.1) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M4 (Apple9) - Apple M4 (10 threads) - 24.00 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe UNUSED_PARAMETER warning doesn't trigger when it should. In both functions the parameter is unused, but it's not detected on the first one.\n\n<img width=\"768\" height=\"614\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c03133da-a457-402c-8474-7d4132c4b44b\" />\n\nMy hypothesis is, that the `pf.nickname` member access confuses the analyzer, because the member happens to have the same name as the parameter. In the second method, I changed the parameter name and the warning is triggered correctly.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nSee the included screenshot / code.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nHere is the code from the screenshot:\n\n```gdscript\nextends Node3D\n\nvar _profiles: Array[PlayerProfile] = []\n\nfunc has_player_nicknamed_1(nickname: String) -> bool:\n\treturn _profiles.any(func(pf: PlayerProfile) -> bool:\n\t\treturn pf.nickname == \"\"\n\t)\n\nfunc has_player_nicknamed_2(nickname_param: String) -> bool:\n\treturn _profiles.any(func(pf: PlayerProfile) -> bool:\n\t\treturn pf.nickname == \"\"\n\t)\n\nclass PlayerProfile extends RefCounted:\n\tvar nickname: String\n```\n\nProject:\n\n[mrp-unused-param.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23962466/mrp-unused-param.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.g